{
  "id": "Compound::DB00987 - Disease::DOID:2531",
  "verbalization": "Cytarabine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Hematologic Cancer through a series of interconnected mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Cytarabine, as a cytotoxic chemotherapeutic agent, is linked to Lymphatic System Cancer, which in turn is associated with Hematologic Cancer through molecular interactions. This relationship is further supported by the association of Tia1 and Tnfrsf8 with Hematologic Cancer, indicating a broader network of molecular pathways that may be influenced by Cytarabine. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role of Cytarabine in modulating cellular processes that contribute to the development of Hematologic Cancer. The evidence underscores a dependency on chemotherapeutic agents that target multiple layers of cellular regulation, suggesting a complex interplay between Cytarabine and hematological malignancies.",
